//? Title: Three Densities, One RealNVP Budget
//? Subtitle: Banana curvature, eight-mode concentration and checkerboard support leakage
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An invertible model can have correct likelihoods and poor generated samples.
This controlled native C++ study fits the same 266-value RealNVP architecture
separately to banana, eight-Gaussian and checkerboard observations. All three
runs retain identical initial weights, batch orders and three-epoch budgets,
with separate stores and Adam states. The complete editable program preserves
all 144 optimizer writes, both actual Jacobians and 3,072 latent-only samples.
Final NLLs are 2.760811806, 3.523986816 and 3.139697790 nats per two-coordinate
row. Only 15.7227% of eight-Gaussian samples lie within three sigma of a mode,
although every mode has a positive count; only 42.5781% of checkerboard samples
lie on its support. Source fidelity and invertibility checks pass while those
quality limitations remain visible.
)
\toc

> Separate density correctness from distribution quality

The native model is the bounded four-coupling RealNVP already developed in the
[affine-coupling report](real_nvp_density.mepml). Each block preserves coordinate
a and changes b to b exp(s(a))+t(a), with s=.8 tanh(raw_scale). Its triangular
Jacobian has log determinant s(a), and inversion uses (b-t(a))exp(-s(a)).
Four alternating 1->16 tanh->2 conditioners plus a positive global diagonal
scale give **266 learned values in 17 tensors**. The Gaussian base yields

$$ \log p_X(x)=-\log(2\pi)-\tfrac12\|f(x)\|^2+\log|\det Df(x)|. $$
\alttext(The observation log density is the Gaussian latent log density plus the forward map log determinant.)

The determinant is recomputed on the current forward or inverse path. The
mathematical inverse has an exact algebraic form; Float32 evaluation still
rounds. A well-implemented bijection guarantees tractable density evaluation,
not that a 48-step fit recovers every mode or a discontinuous support boundary.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/study_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::Diagram d(28,1150);
 dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;s.width=10;s.height=5;s.font_size=32;
 d.node("data",{-24,0},"3 analytic families\nExplicit Gaussian triples",s)
 .node("fits",{-11,0},"3 separate RealNVPs\nSame weights / budget",s)
 .node("density",{2,0},"Gaussian likelihood\nActual Jacobian checks",s)
 .node("samples",{15,0},"Invert all prior rows\nNo data feedback",s)
 .node("quality",{28,0},"Curvature / modes\nSupport leakage",s)
 .edge("data","fits").edge("fits","density").edge("density","samples").edge("samples","quality")
 .save_svg("build/study_method.svg");
}
