// result_end

\caption(Each panel shows all three validation records, one final test model score and four test baselines. Vertical limits differ so each table/curve can be read; numerical comparisons use the table.)
\alttext(Banana validation dips at epoch two then rises; ring and checker validation decrease. The ring and checker model NLLs remain well above analytic truth.)

The banana model improves over its full Gaussian baseline 2.837374308, but
its curvature moment remains.719403856 instead of the true expectation 1.
The eight-mode model's NLL is only slightly below the Gaussian 3.530117592,
far from truth .961499012. Checkerboard NLL is slightly worse than the full
Gaussian 3.139320070, with truth 2.079441542. No significance interval or broad
ranking claim follows from one short fit and 128 held-out observations.

> Compare each true and learned PDF without hiding support zeros

Each pair retains all 128² source grid centers on[-4,4]². Source rows descend
in y; plotting reverses storage order to keep physical y upward. Both panels
of a family use the same native terrain palette and limits: 0 to 0.2 for banana
and checker,0 to 1 for the ring. Square cells preserve geometry. The finite
window is a display, not a claim of unit probability within the box.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/study_density.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
