> Measure concentration and leakage instead of counting modes alone

All diagnostics are computed for every fitted family. Nearest ring centers use
Double hypot; strict comparisons choose the first exact tie. Count a sample
when distance<=.45 (three component standard deviations). Eight positive counts
only establishes visitation: the ring fit covers all eight modes but puts just
161/1024 samples within that radius. Checker support fraction is 436/1024;
588 generated points fall outside the valid cells. Its smooth bijective flow
cannot exactly reproduce disconnected zero-density regions. The budget also
leaves a large empirical mismatch. Banana curvature is mean[y(x²−1)], with
true expectation 1. No rejection, filtering or post-fit correction changes the
saved samples or scores.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/study_quality.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{37,99,235},{234,88,12},{22,163,74}};int i=0;
 std::print("| Fitted family | Checker support | Ring fraction within.45 | Modes covered | Banana moment |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
 for(auto family:{"banana","eight_gaussians","checkerboard"}){n::Tensor samples;for(auto& [k,v]:n::load_npz(std::string("build/flow_density_2d/")+family+"/samples.npz"))if(k=="samples")samples=v;
 auto d=n::models::FlowStudySampleDiagnostics(samples);auto x=n::arange(0,8).to_vector<double>(),y=d.mode_counts.to_vector<double>();p.lines(x,y,family,colors[i]).points(x,y,"",colors[i++],4);
 std::print("|{}|{:.12f}|{:.12f}|{}|{:.12f}|\n",family,d.checkerboard_support_fraction,d.fraction_near_modes,d.modes_covered,d.banana_curvature_moment);}
 p.y_limits(0,65).x_label("Nearest ring center index").y_label("Number of samples within.45").title("Every family visits all modes; concentration remains low").save_svg("build/study_quality.svg");
}
