|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
|banana|0.418945312500|0.134765625000|8|0.719403856091|
|eight_gaussians|0.342773437500|0.157226562500|8|-0.127649721802|
|checkerboard|0.425781250000|0.139648437500|8|0.056048572561|
\image(figures/study_quality.svg)
// result_end

\caption(All 24 counts are shown without normalization or pooling across fits. Ring-fitted counts sum 161, leaving 863 samples farther than three sigma from every mode. Coverage 8/8 is compatible with this poor concentration.)
\alttext(Three colored eight-point count profiles are positive at every mode; a table separately gives concentration, checker support and curvature.)

> Check per-point volume changes, both actual Jacobians and normalization

The next figure retains both analytic and actual log determinants on all 128
held-out points and all 1,024 inverse samples per family. Forward and inverse
have their own row ordering; their profiles are not corresponding pairs.
Reverse-mode derivatives of both output coordinates determine the actual 2x2
Jacobians. Positive determinants, per-point cancellation on reconstruction,
roundtrips, bit-exact restore, repeated samples and immutable inference are
checked by the complete program. Source phase probes additionally retain every
gradient, post-write weight and optimizer iteration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/study_volume.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(3,2);
 for(auto family:{"banana","eight_gaussians","checkerboard"}){std::string root=std::string("build/flow_density_2d/")+family+"/";std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> o,s,v;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz(root+"outputs.npz"))o[k]=x;for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz(root+"samples.npz"))s[k]=x;for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz(root+"plot_values.npz"))v[k]=x;
 for(bool inverse:{false,true}){auto analytic=inverse?s.at("inverse_logdet"):o.at("forward_logdet"),actual=v.at(inverse?"inverse_actual_logdet":"actual_logdet");auto axis=n::arange(0,analytic.size(0)).to_vector<double>();
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points(axis,analytic.to_vector<double>(),"Analytic path",{37,99,235},3).points(axis,actual.to_vector<double>(),"Actual Jacobian",{234,88,12},1)
 .margins(72,22,54,64).y_limits(-1.1,1.6).x_label("Row index in its own pool").y_label("Log absolute determinant").title(std::string(family)+(inverse?":inverse1024":":forward128"));layout.add(p);}}
 layout.size(1100,1500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/study_volume.svg");
}
